course: dictionary
lesson: 7332
title: Plankton: tiny drifters of the sea
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Plankton are tiny living things that drift in the sea and in lakes, carried along by the water. Most are too small to see without a microscope. Plankton is a noun, and it is uncountable: we say some plankton, not two planktons.
explain: There are two kinds. Plant plankton make their own food from sunlight, and they make a large share of the oxygen we breathe. Animal plankton include tiny shrimps and baby fish. «Plankton makes much of Earth's oxygen», so the air you breathe was partly made by tiny plants.
explain: Read the clues around the word. «Plankton are tiny drifting living things» tells you they are small and float rather than swim fast. «Oil and gas come from tiny sea plankton buried in mud» tells you plankton can be left in the mud for a very long time. Swap your meaning into the sentence to check it fits.
fact: Plankton means tiny living things that drift in water.
fact: Plant plankton make food from sunlight and give us much of our oxygen.
fact: Animal plankton include tiny shrimps and baby fish.
fact: Plankton is uncountable, so say some plankton, not a plankton.
fact: Plankton feed small fish and krill, and the blue whale eats mostly tiny krill.
exercise: «Plankton are tiny drifting living things.» What does drifting mean here? | Sinking fast to the bottom | *Being carried slowly along by water | Swimming very quickly | Growing into a big fish
exercise: «Plankton makes much of Earth's oxygen.» Which kind of plankton makes its own food from sunlight? | Animal plankton | *Plant plankton | Oil and gas | Whale poo
exercise: Ella says plankton are big fish that swim fast. Which statement is correct? | Plankton only live in hot deserts | *Plankton are tiny drifting living things, and most are too small to see | Plankton are large fish that swim fast | Plankton are rocks on the sea floor
test: Which of these is an example of animal plankton? | Oak tree | *Tiny shrimp | Pebble | Cloud
test: Plankton are mostly too small to see without what? | *A microscope | A ladder | Glasses for reading | A torch
exam: Which statement about plankton is true? | *Plankton are tiny living things that drift in the sea and in lakes | Plankton are a kind of rock | Plankton are only found in deserts | Plankton are huge animals that stay still on the sea floor
